      "message": "An alternative that would avoid having to update the RenderStep and DrawPass code (and would match the end state we want when we consolidate to a single binding), would be to have `PipelineDataGatherer` track its active UniformManager.\n\nAfter `resetForDraw()`, the active manager is `fPaintUniformManager`, and after `endPaintData()` it switches to `fRenderStepUniformManager`. It stays with that manager even after `rewindForRenderStep()` and `endRenderStepData()`, since any future recorded uniforms would still be for a different render step.",
